  "summary": "Preprints present faster RNA folding sampling in memerna, AlphaFold-scale motif annotation, and EHR-molecular diagnosis matching.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a computational orientation: each converts a large search space into an inferred biological property. The lead item introduces iterative sampling, a deterministic algorithm that enumerates RNA secondary structures in order of increasing free energy, implemented in memerna for cotranscriptional folding. ActSeekN applies a related logic to protein structure, searching catalytic structural motifs against an AlphaFold-derived active-site database and transferring function from matched sites. DxFit is the least structural of the set, using an ensemble approach over EHR ICD codes and diagnosis descriptions to identify diagnoses consistent with a molecular finding for rare genetic disorders. What is new is the emphasis on deterministic enumeration and scalable database-driven transfer. Quantitative performance claims in the RNA item are not reproduced here.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-30"
}
